      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PHYSICAL QUANTITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Physical quantities are classified into Fundamental (independent) and Derived (dependent) quantities.",
        "The SI system consists of 7 fundamental units (metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, mole, candela) and 2 supplementary units (radian, steradian).",
        "Density is calculated as Mass divided by Volume, with the standard SI unit being kg/m³.",
        "Dimensional formulas express physical quantities using fundamental base dimensions [M], [L], and [T].",
        "Dimensional analysis is used to check the correctness of equations and convert units between different systems."
      ],
      "id": "0imlb88"
